<title>FRANCE: French Feb consumer sentiment rises.</title>
<headline>French Feb consumer sentiment rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>INSEE gave the following data on household opinions. A positive figure shows the percentage points by which the percentage of respondents saying things had improved or risen outnumbered the percentage saying the opposite.</p>
<p>				    Feb  Jan  Dec  Nov  Oct  Sep  Jul</p>
<p> Overall Confidence	   -29  -30  -33  -34  -34  -36  -35</p>
<p> Past living standards	-63  -68  -66  -69  -71  -72  -73</p>
<p> Future living standards    -34  -34  -38  -39  -39  -44  -43</p>
<p> Future unemployment	   49   61   54   66   70   76   76</p>
<p> Past inflation		 -48  -42  -53  -53  -52  -54  -47</p>
<p> Future inflation	     -38  -33  -37  -34  -36  -37  -44</p>
<p> Good time to spend	   -23  -23  -25  -29  -31  -34  -32</p>
<p> Good time to save	     52   52   51   54   54   53   50</p>
<p> Ability to save		-26  -30  -29  -27  -29  -31  -30</p>
<p> Current personal finances   10   10    9    9    6    9    9</p>
<p> Past personal finances     -19  -20  -21  -22  -23  -23  -23</p>
<p> Future personal finances    -5   -6   -8   -8   -8  -10  -10</p>
<p>INSEE does not publish a consumer sentiment survey in August.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
